.TH BASTION 1 "" "bastion 1.5.25" "Bastion Manual"
.SH NAME
bastion \- modular, layered Linux firewall framework
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bastion
[\fB\-\-version\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bastion is a modular, layered Linux firewall framework built on nftables. It provides an operator CLI, an optional AI analysis layer, and a guided setup wizard, and secures the full spectrum of hosts \(em a defense\-in\-depth endpoint, a routing edge firewall, or a server that already runs another firewall manager (libvirt, Docker).
.PP
Configuration lives in \fI/etc/bastion/machine.conf\fR; \fBbastion generate\fR renders it into the live config files. See \fBbastion \fICOMMAND\fB \-\-help\fR for the exact flags of any command.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS setup
interactive setup wizard (detect, configure, install)
.PP
\fBbastion setup\fR [options]
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
walk the wizard, show what would be written; write nothing, no API calls
.TP
\fB\-\-profile PROFILE\fR
skip profile selection (full\-edge|basic\-edge|full\-endpoint|minimal\-endpoint|custom)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-ai\fR
exclude the L3 AI layer from the install (no API key prompt, no edge\-ai units) \(em the rest of the profile is unaffected
.TP
\fB\-\-stage\-only\fR
write + generate the config but do NOT load the firewall or install layers; review it, then apply behind `bastion switch`'s deadman
.TP
\fB\-\-bootstrap\fR
soft recovery: re\-detect from scratch, do NOT trust the existing machine.conf for detected values, and show where it disagrees with the live system (e.g. a wrong SSH port that locked you out)
.TP
\fB\-\-set KEY=VALUE\fR
set a config answer non\-interactively (overrides detection + prompts); repeatable, e.g. \-\-set trusted_hosts=10.0.0.2 \-\-set ssh_port=1111
.TP
\fB\-\-root ROOT\fR
operate under this base dir instead of / (staged preview/testing)
.SS generate
resolve templates \-> config files
.PP
\fBbastion generate\fR [options]
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
validate all placeholders resolve; write nothing, make no network calls
.TP
\fB\-\-conf CONF\fR
path to machine.conf (default: standard search order)
.TP
\fB\-\-templates TEMPLATES\fR
path to templates/ dir (default: cwd or package dir)
.TP
\fB\-\-out OUT\fR
write under this base dir instead of / (for testing/dry\-run)
.SS status
show layer install/active state
.PP
\fBbastion status\fR [options]
.TP
\fB\-\-health\fR
also run each layer's health checks
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
emit the machine\-readable status projection
.TP
\fB\-\-conf CONF\fR
path to machine.conf
.TP
\fB\-\-root ROOT\fR
inspect under this base dir instead of / (chroot/bootstrap/testing)
.SS tui
read\-only terminal dashboard (layers, sets, AI, audit)
.PP
\fBbastion tui\fR [options]
.TP
\fB\-\-conf CONF\fR
path to machine.conf
.TP
\fB\-\-root ROOT\fR
inspect under this base dir instead of / (testing)
.SS state
emit the canonical world\-state JSON document (the TUI/GUI contract)
.PP
\fBbastion state\fR [options]
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
(default) machine\-readable JSON document
.TP
\fB\-\-compact\fR
single\-line JSON instead of indented
.TP
\fB\-\-conf CONF\fR
path to machine.conf
.TP
\fB\-\-templates TEMPLATES\fR
templates dir (for the drift section)
.TP
\fB\-\-root ROOT\fR
inspect under this base dir instead of / (testing)
.SS config
view/change machine.conf settings (the control room)
.PP
\fBbastion config\fR {list | get | describe | set} [options]
.TP
\fBbastion config list\fR
