.SS zones
manage [zones] source\->action input\-accept rules
.PP
\fBbastion zones\fR \fI{list | add | remove}\fR \fIname\fR \fIsource\fR \fIaction\fR [options]
.TP
\fB{list | add | remove}\fR
\&
.TP
\fBname\fR
zone name (add/remove)
.TP
\fBsource\fR
any | <IP/CIDR> | iface:NAME | iface:NAME+<CIDR> (add)
.TP
\fBaction\fR
all | a port list e.g. 8096 53/udp (add)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
preview the rule delta + clobber check; write and reload nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
proceed even if the live kernel has unmanaged rules the reload would flush
.TP
\fB\-\-conf CONF\fR
\&
.TP
\fB\-\-root ROOT\fR
\&
.SS layer
manage an individual layer
.PP
\fBbastion layer\fR \fI{status | install | uninstall | enable | disable}\fR \fIname\fR [options]
.TP
\fB{status | install | uninstall | enable | disable}\fR
status/install/uninstall a layer; enable/disable also add/remove it from [machine] layers in machine.conf
.TP
\fBname\fR
layer id, e.g. l0
.TP
\fB\-\-conf CONF\fR
path to machine.conf
.TP
\fB\-\-root ROOT\fR
operate under this base dir instead of / (staged install/testing)
.TP
\fB\-\-templates TEMPLATES\fR
path to templates/ dir
.TP
\fB\-\-scripts SCRIPTS\fR
path to scripts/ dir
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
bypass the prerequisite/dependency check (e.g. force\-uninstall l0 while dependent layers remain)
.SS firewall
