.TP
\fB\-\-conf CONF\fR
path to machine.conf
.TP
\fB\-\-root ROOT\fR
operate under this base dir instead of /
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
Most commands accept \fB\-\-root \fIDIR\fR (operate under a staged tree instead of \fI/\fR, touching no live kernel or systemd state) and \fB\-\-conf \fIPATH\fR (use a specific machine.conf). Read\-only inspection commands accept \fB\-\-json\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/etc/bastion/machine.conf\fR
Per\-machine configuration (topology, zones, layer selection). Never contains secrets.
.TP
\fI/etc/bastion/machine.env\fR
Flat variables rendered from machine.conf, read by the operational scripts.
.TP
\fI/etc/nftables.conf\fR
The rendered ruleset. Fully rewritten by \fBbastion generate\fR \(em do not hand\-edit; put rules in \fB[zones]\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation at \fIhttps://github.com/indyfive11/bastion\fR, including the getting\-started guide, command reference, and troubleshooting docs.
.SH AUTHOR
The Bastion project.
